# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# ChainTrace AI - what lives in git and what does not
#
# The bundled dataset under data/synthetic/, the offline GeoIP table and the sample
# upload are tracked *on purpose*: they are deterministic from RANDOM_SEED = 42 and
# they are the exact input every measured number in the README was produced from, so
# a reviewer can read the evidence without running anything first.
#
# Everything below is either a virtualenv, a secret, or a file that the image build
# regenerates in a few seconds (scripts/train_models.py, scripts/run_full_pipeline.py).
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# virtualenvs and caches
.venv/
.venv311/
venv/
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.pytest_cache/

# OS / editor / scratch
.DS_Store
*.log
.tmp_pdf/

# secrets - never commit
.env
.streamlit/secrets.toml

# regenerated by the Docker build and by the pipeline
data/models/*.joblib
data/models/*.json
data/artifacts/
data/evidence_ledger.jsonl
